
🖥 System Information & Access

uname → Identify OS type

uptime → System running time

who, whoami → Logged-in users

which docker / java → Locate executable binary in use

id → User ID & group ID

sudo → Run administrative commands

sudo shutdown now → Shutdown system safely



📦 Package Management

apt / apt-get → Install, update, remove packages

sudo apt-get update → Refresh package list

sudo apt remove docker.io → Uninstall packages

Other Linux distros use:

 yum, dnf, pacman, rpm



👥 User & Group Management

sudo useradd -m username → Create user + home directory

sudo passwd username → Set user password

su username → Switch user

exit → Return to previous user

cat /etc/passwd → View users

sudo userdel username → Delete user



Groups

sudo groupadd groupName (to create group)

cat /etc/group  (to check the groups created)

Sudo gpasswd -a UserName GroupName (to add the user in specific group -a flag stands for add)

Sudo gpasswd -M Username1, UserName2, UserName3 (to add multiple user in a group with single command)

sudo groupdel groupName (to delete a group)



🔐 File Permissions & Ownership

ls -l → Check permissions

drwxrwxr-x → Directory | User | Group | Others

chmod 777 file → Full access (⚠ avoid in production)

umask → Default permission settings

sudo chown user file → Change file owner

chgrp group file → Change group ownership


